# Checkout-only settings for the Makefile's web targets. `relay/setup.sh` copies
# this file to `.env` the first time it runs in a checkout, and nothing in it has
# to be edited to run the relay.
WEB_PROJECT=herdr-mobile-relay
# WEB_BRANCH=main

# Optional, for non-interactive `make web-deploy` authentication. Keep the ignored
# `.env` file at mode 0600 when it holds a token.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# The relay never reads this file, and you never have to write the relay's own
# environment by hand: setup generates the relay token, the instance id, the
# tunnel configuration path, and the gateway entries the connection chooser
# records, into `relay/.env` for a checkout or the Herdr plugin configuration
# directory for an installation. Both are created at mode 0600, and setup only
# fills in what is missing.
#
# Every other variable the relay reads has a built-in default. Add one to that
# generated file only to override it:
#
#   HERDR_GATEWAY_URL=              Gateway base URL, for example
#                                   wss://gw.example.com, or several separated by
#                                   commas. Empty (the default) keeps the
#                                   Cloudflare tunnel path; setting it makes Quick
#                                   Start skip cloudflared entirely.
#                                   Self-hosting: docs/gateway-self-hosting.md.
#   HERDR_GATEWAY_SELECTION=ordered How the relay picks among healthy gateways.
#                                   ordered (the default) takes the first healthy
#                                   HERDR_GATEWAY_URL entry in configured order;
#                                   latency keeps the lowest-latency healthy one.
#   HERDR_WEBRTC_UDP_PORT=0         Fixed UDP port for the direct WebRTC path.
#                                   0 (default) picks an ephemeral port.
#   HERDR_REACHABILITY_PORT_MAPPING=1
#                                   Ask the router for a UPnP/NAT-PMP mapping for
#                                   the WebRTC port, raising direct-path success.
#                                   Default 1; set 0 to never talk to the router.
#   HERDR_TRANSPORT_FORCE_RELAY=0   Test flag: 1 disables the direct WebRTC
#                                   upgrade and keeps every frame on the gateway
#                                   path. Default 0.
#   HERDR_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIRS=       Extra Claude Code config dirs, colon-separated
#                                   (the platform path-list separator, as in PATH;
#                                   a path containing a literal colon can't be
#                                   listed this way), added to the ~/.claude
#                                   default. See README.md: "Agents with a
#                                   non-default config directory".
#   HERDR_QODER_CONFIG_DIRS=        Same, for Qoder CLI; added to ~/.qoder.
#   HERDR_CODEX_CONFIG_DIRS=        Same, for Codex; added to ~/.codex.
#   HERDR_PI_CONFIG_DIRS=           Same, for Pi; added to ~/.pi/agent.
#   HERDR_OMP_CONFIG_DIRS=          Same, for Oh My Pi; added to ~/.omp/agent.
